SUMMARY:Deadline: Craigardan Trillium Fellowship 2027 (residency for artist
 s\, activists and scholars of color\, USD 4\,600 + USD 500 honorarium)
DESCRIPTION:The Trillium Fellowship supports artists\, activists and schola
 rs of color working in any discipline who would benefit from the time and 
 space to pursue their work or find creative retreat at Craigardan\, a resi
 dency and farm in the Adirondacks. One Trillium fellowship is awarded each
  year\, need-based\, by invitation or application (nominations accepted).\
 n\nOrganisation: Craigardan\nLocation: Elizabethtown\, New York\, USA (Adi
 rondack Park). In person\; rural\, car recommended.\nAward: USD 4\,600 fel
 lowship toward a minimum two-week residency (covers the residency fee)\, p
 lus a USD 500 honorarium. Travel\, materials and personal expenses are not
  covered. USD 25 application fee (waivers available on request).\nDuration
 : Minimum two weeks\, during the summer season (May to October 2027)\n\nMo
 re: https://craigardan.org/fellowships?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://craigardan.org/fellowships?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Elizabethtown\, New York\, USA (Adirondack Park). In person\; rura
 l\, car recommended.
END:VEVENT
