 28 (Hutchins Center\, Harvard\; USD 70\,000 to 75\,000 for the academic ye
 ar)
DESCRIPTION:The Fellows Program is the oldest activity of the W. E. B. Du B
 ois Research Institute\, which has appointed fellows since 1975. It invite
 s up to twenty scholars to be in residence each year\, reflecting the inte
 rdisciplinary breadth of African and African American Studies\, and suppor
 ts research at both the predoctoral and postdoctoral levels.\n\nOrganisati
 on: W. E. B. Du Bois Research Institute\, Hutchins Center for African and 
 African American Research\, Harvard University\nLocation: Hutchins Center\
 , Harvard University\, Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (in residence)\nAwa
 rd: Stipends of USD 70\,000 to USD 75\,000 for the ten-month academic year
 \, adjusted for one-semester fellowships. Health insurance is not provided
 . No application fee.\nDuration: Ten-month academic year 2027-28\, or one 
 semester\n\nMore: https://hutchinscenter.fas.harvard.edu/apply?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
